<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Suleyman II of Eshref</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1326</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Suleyman II was the last bey of the Eshrefids, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beysehir">Beyşehir</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. In 1326 he was executed by Timurtash, the Ilkhanid governor of Anatolia, who was reasserting Mongol authority over the beyliks, and his lands passed to the neighbouring Hamidids.</p></div>
